import Erdos993Lean.ZhangKernel.Core

/-!
# Kernel-checked finite part: check items of the orders 47 (generated)

For every `(n, a)` of these orders, `items_n_a` lists the check items of `k = 1, …,
⌊(2a+1)/3⌋ − 1` (2974 weighted rows in total).  Generated by the lane-K scratch script
`gen_all.lean` (campaign `ProofRuns/2026-09-28_analytic_large_n`, `LEAN/lanes/K/scratch/`),
which evaluates the package's own functions: the stored certificates of the order `n` are
parsed from `ZhangCertX.dataFor n` by `ZhangCertX.parseEntries (ZhangCertX.tokens ·)` and
looked up by `ZhangCertX.lookup`; a separator `p/q` becomes the generic certificate
`gen .cond q [(.assumption k, p)]` and a linear certificate the generic certificate
`ZhangCertX.linearToGeneric` (the author's normalization (39)), exactly as
`ZhangCertX.storedOK` checks them; a triple without a stored certificate gets `direct h`,
`h` the first direct criterion of `ZhangCertX.directOK` that passes (`0` the path row, `1` the
lower layer rule, `2` the upper layer rule).  The generator's output has SHA-256
`305c0beb46e516e41a563ebc8dd8a17d3ba1763c67cff82bd29ab60c0b96523a`.

The items carry no trust: the soundness of `checkAV` (`ZhangKernel/Sound.lean`) holds for
arbitrary items.
-/

namespace Erdos993Lean

namespace ZhangKernel

open ZhangCertX

set_option maxRecDepth 20000

